    "input": "search_document: Based on the handbook excerpts provided, here is the assessment of your return request:\n\n**1. Return Window Eligibility**\nThe handbook states that you have a \"strict 30-day window from the date of delivery to initiate a return request\" and that if you miss this deadline, the item cannot be accepted back [returns]. It further clarifies that the return window is \"exactly 30 days from the delivery date\" [returns]. Since you stated it has been \"exactly 30 days\" since the package arrived, you are technically still within the allowable window to initiate the request, provided you do so before the day ends. The policy does not specify a time-of-day cutoff, only the day count [returns].\n\n**2. Item Condition and Restocking Fee**\nYou mentioned the bike is in \"perfect condition with all the original packaging\" and that you only test-ridden it in the driveway. The handbook requires returned items to be in \"original, unused condition with all tags, manuals, and protective packaging intact\" [returns]. It specifies that a 15% restocking fee is deducted if the item shows \"signs of wear, dirt, or damage\" [returns]. Since you report no wear, dirt, or damage, and the packaging is intact, you should not be subject to the 15% restocking fee, assuming the inspection confirms the \"unused\" status [returns].\n\n**3. Shipping Costs**\nYou offered to cover return shipping costs. The handbook states that standard ground shipping costs for returns are the customer\u2019s responsibility [returns]. You can use a prepaid return label for a flat fee of $12.50, or if you choose an expedited carrier, you must pay the full cost upfront and will only be reimbursed the standard rate [returns].\n\n**4. Important Note on \"Custom-Configured\" Bikes**\nThe handbook explicitly states: \"We do not accept returns on custom-configured bikes or personalized gear... If you ordered the wrong size or color, you are responsible for the full cost of the item, which is non-refundable\" [returns].\n*   **Action Required:** You must verify if your mountain bike was a standard off-the-shelf model or a \"custom-configured\" bike. If it was custom-configured (made to order), it is **non-returnable** regardless of the condition or the 30-day window [returns]. If it was a standard model, the return is permissible under the conditions above.\n\n**Summary of Next Steps:**\n1.  **Verify Bike Type:** Confirm if the bike is standard or custom-configured. If custom, the return will be denied [returns].\n2.  **Initiate Return Immediately:** If it is a standard bike, log into your account and initiate the return request today to ensure it is processed within the 30-day window [returns].\n3.  **Prepare Item:** Ensure all tags, manuals, and packaging are intact [returns].\n4.  **Shipping:** Purchase the $12.50 prepaid label or arrange your own shipping, understanding that you are responsible for these costs [returns].\n5.  **Refund Timeline:** Once received and inspected, refunds are processed within 5 business days, with funds appearing in your account 3\u20137 business days later (up to 10 days for credit cards) [returns].\n\nIf the bike is custom-configured, or if you are unable to initiate the return within the strict 30-day limit, I can offer to escalate the ticket to a human agent to see if any exceptions can be made, though the handbook states the deadline is \"non-negotiable\" [returns].",
